From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lukasz <lukasz@VM>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: airoha: Add AN7552 cpufreq compatible

The cpufreq node in an7563.dtsi is named "airoha,an7552-cpufreq", but
airoha_cpu_pmdomain_of_match only lists an7583 and en7581.  Nothing
matches the node, so no genpd provider is registered for it and every
power-domain lookup against it fails.  cpufreq-dt then returns
-EPROBE_DEFER forever, because the deferral comes from the OPP table's
required-opps resolving through that domain:

    platform cpufreq-dt: deferred probe pending: (reason unknown)

The "reason unknown" is the missing piece to look for: nothing in the
deferred-probe machinery ever ran to attach an error to this device, so
the record carries no reason to report.

AN7563 and AN7552 are the same core with the cpufreq domain in the same
place, so listing the compatible alongside the other two is all that is
needed for the domain to probe and cpufreq-dt to come up.

Signed-off-by: lukasz <lukasz@VM>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/airoha-cpu-pmdomain.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/airoha-cpu-pmdomain.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/airoha-cpu-pmdomain.c
@@ -124,6 +124,7 @@ static void airoha_cpu_pmdomain_remove(struct p
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id airoha_cpu_pmdomain_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "airoha,an7552-cpufreq" },
 	{ .compatible = "airoha,an7583-cpufreq" },
 	{ .compatible = "airoha,en7581-cpufreq" },
 	{ },
 };
